# docs/KEYMAP.md §Board and card detail — "Board filtering keeps horizontal navigation on keys
# the input does not own": `left` / `right` move the caret through `FleetTextInput`, so column
# navigation while the board filter has the keyboard is `Tab` / `Shift-Tab`.
#
# `scenarios/board/filter.scenario` pins that `/` takes the keyboard without opening an overlay
# and that the two-stage `Esc` holds; this one pins the split those two key pairs make, which is
# the regression a migrated input invites: a `left` that walks columns eats the caret, and a
# `Tab` that inserts a tab loses the column cursor.
#
# The oracles are `lists.board.selected.label` for the focused column and `lists.board.filter`
# for the query — the board mirrors both into `AppState`, so both can be waited on. A caret
# motion changes no text, so where the next character lands is the proof that the caret moved.
#
# Paste is deliberately not exercised: `clipboard set` and `clipboard get` fail in every lane by
# design (`docs/TESTING-HARNESS.md` §1); the kit's own gpui tests cover `cmd-v`.
#
# No `shot`: this is a keyboard scenario, so it belongs in the headless subset too (§7).
fixture: board
await idle 20000
key g b
await hub_tab == Board 10000
assert lists.board.selected.label == "Backlog" && focused == "board.column[0].card[0]"

key /
await focused == "board.filter" 5000
assert mode == "Filter" && key_contexts[1] == "BoardFilter" && overlay absent
type card
await lists.board.filter == card 5000

# `Tab` and `Shift-Tab` move the focused column while the input keeps the keyboard and the
# query keeps its text.
key tab
await lists.board.selected.label == "Todo" 5000
assert focused == "board.filter" && lists.board.filter == card
key tab
await lists.board.selected.label == "In Progress" 5000
key shift-tab
await lists.board.selected.label == "Todo" 5000
assert focused == "board.filter" && mode == "Filter"

# `left` and `right` are the caret's, not the column's: the column stays on `Todo` and the next
# character lands where the caret was left.
key left left
type X
await lists.board.filter == "caXrd" 5000
assert lists.board.selected.label == "Todo"
key right
type Y
await lists.board.filter == "caXrYd" 5000
assert lists.board.selected.label == "Todo" && focused == "board.filter"
dump edited

# The two-stage `Esc` still ends it: the first press leaves the input keeping the filter, the
# second clears it, and the column the `Tab`s chose is still the focused one.
key escape
await focused != "board.filter" 5000
assert lists.board.filter == "caXrYd" && key_contexts[1] == "Board"
key escape
await lists.board.filter == "" 5000
assert lists.board.selected.label == "Todo" && key_contexts[0] == "Hub"
dump cleared
quit
